\**{c=red:Note:}** Missions 3-3 to 5-2 can be done with any {z:Nation}, as they are all ultimately the same. (They will require cutscenes in their own cities, but the bulk of the work is identical for each.)
=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough {p:Crystals|Crystal} (3+ if you skipped the previous mission) to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the {n:Gate Guard}.
* Check the **Vestal Chamber door** at the top of {z:Heavens Tower} for a cutscene with the {p:Star Sibyl}. You will receive {@k} {k:Letter to the ambassador}.
* Speak with {n:Pakh Jatalfih} at the **Windurstian Embassy** in {z:Ru'Lude Gardens} (I-9) for a cutscene.
* Head to {z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower} using the {p:Survival Guide} teleportation, {p:Outpost} warp, or {p:Home Point} warp.
* You will now likely need to climb to the 10th floor of {z:Delkfutt's Tower|Upper Delkfutt's Tower} in order to gain a {@i:Delkfutt Key|549} {i:Delkfutt Key|Delkfutt Key|549} in order to access the Basement of the Tower:
** If you already possess the {@i:Delkfutt Key|549} {i:Delkfutt Key|Delkfutt Key|549} (trade it to the door) or the {@k} {k:Delkfutt key} (no trading needed) then you may skip this climb:
*** Head to {z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower} (E-8) Map 1 and enter the Basement by clicking the **Cermet Door**. Once you go through the door, proceed to (L-7) and click the **Cermet Door** for a cutscene. (**Note:** Another player using a key does not work.)
*** Return to the **Windurstian Embassy** in {z:Ru'Lude Gardens} and click the **Door: Windurstian Emb.** for a cutscene to complete the Mission.
**** This is the 3rd door inside the embassy building. There are multiple doors with the same name.
** If you do not possess the Key, start the climb process detailed below:
*** You may be {s:Tractored|Tractor} through this **Basement** door without the Key. If you decide to go this route, proceed to the "**Obtaining Delkfutt Key Short Way**" section.
*** Otherwise, read the "**Obtaining Delkfutt Key Long Way**" section.

=2 Obtaining Delkfutt Key Short Way
This is the shortest route. You may be {s:Tractored|Tractor} through the door to the Basement at {z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower} (E-8) Map 1 without the Key if a party member already has it.
* Next, you can open the door at (J-8).
* Click it to travel to {z:Upper Delkfutt's Tower}. Walk forward then click the **???** at the bottom of the stairs to be teleported directly to:
* {m:Porphyrion}, kill this NM then trade the {@i:Delkfutt Key|549} {i:Delkfutt Key|Delkfutt Key|549} it drops to the Elevator directly beside it.
** Interacting with the ??? that appears shortly after vanquishing {m:Porphyrion} also rewards the player with the {@k} {k:Delkfutt key}.
* After using the elevator, proceed down the spiral stair case for two zones, through the **Cermet Door** in Map 5 at (I-9) {z:Upper Delkfutt's Tower}.
* Skip to the "**Finishing the Mission**" section below.

=2 Obtaining Delkfutt Key Long Way
This process involves a multi-zone, ten-floor run up the entire tower. Expect the climb up alone to take roughly 15 minutes. If you are below level 50, consider bringing the following:
* {s:Sneak}/{p:Invisible (Status)} or {@i:Prism Powder|4164} {i:Prism Powder|Prism Powder|4164}/{@i:Silent Oil|4165} {i:Silent Oil|Silent Oil|4165}.
* Some form of {p:Reraise} and {p:Warp} is also helpful.

Set your {p:Home Point} in {p:Jeuno} if you plan on warping out after the Mission.
* A {k:Map of Qufim Island} and a {k:Map of Delkfutt's Tower} may be purchased from {n:Promurouve} at (H-7) in {z:Lower Jeuno} (inside the building) or {n:Rusese} at (H-6) in {z:Upper Jeuno} for 600 and 650 {p:Gil} respectively.
* Make your way to {z:Port Jeuno} and zone into {z:Qufim Island}.
* Enter {z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower} at (F-6).
* Once inside prepare for a long walk. {p:Bats|Category:Bat} and {m:Dancing Weapons|Dancing Weapon} will aggro to {@a:Sound|Detects by Sound} Sound and {p:Goblins|Category:Goblin} and {p:Giants|Category:Gigas} will aggro to {@a:Sight|Detects by Sight} Sight. {p:Pots|Category:Magic Pot} and {p:Dolls|Category:Doll} are Aggressive to {@a:Magic|Detects by Magic} Magic.

=3 Navigation
* **Floor 1:** ({z:Lower Delkfutt's Tower})
** Enter and follow the right wall until you reach the stairs at (E/F-6).
* **Floor 2:**
** Follow the left wall until you reach the stairs at (I-9).
* **Floor 3:**
** Follow the right wall until you reach the **Teleporter** at (G-6).
* **Floor 4:** ({z:Middle Delkfutt's Tower} Map 1)
** Follow the right wall past 2 **Teleporters** and go up the stairs at (J-6).
* **Floor 5:** (half way there)
** Enter the door into a hallway on your right at (I-7) then follow the left wall until you see a stairway leading north at (H-10).
* **Floor 6:**
** At the top of the stairs follow the right wall to a **Teleporter** at (J-10).
* **Floor 7:**
** In this big room head north-west to a stairway at (G-7).
* **Floor 8:**
** Follow the left wall to another stairway at (J-7).
* **Floor 9:**
** Head south (the only way you can go) to a stairway that leads back down at (J-10).
* **Floor 8:** (again)
** Head west to a stairway leading back up at (G-10). Do not fall down the hole in the floor! If you do, then it's a one-way trip back to floor 7.
* **Floor 9:** (again)
** Follow the left wall until you reach a **Teleporter** at (F-6).
* **Floor 10:** ({z:Upper Delkfutt's Tower} Map 1)
** When you zone in head through the door to the south-east and down a hallway. You will find a door on your right at (H-7). This door is guarded by {m:Mimas}, a {m:Gigas} NM that uses {p:Hundred Fists}.
** After killing {m:Mimas} and clearing the hallway (or just walking past them, the door's not locked), enter the door at (H-7) into a large room. This room will be filled with {m:Gigas} and a NM named {m:Porphyrion}.
*** Try to pull {m:Porphyrion} out into the hallway without linking any of the other {m:Gigas}. {p:Summoner} or a high level helper is useful for this.
* Kill {m:Porphyrion} and any aggro you may have. {m:Porphyrion} will drop 6 {@i:Delkfutt Key|549} {i:Delkfutt Key|Delkfutt Key|549}s - these will be distributed among your party. Each player can only hold 1 key, so any excess will trigger error messages. If your group needs more than 6 keys, you will have to wait 10 minutes for Porphyrion to respawn.
** After defeating {m:Porphyrion}, you may choose to head up two more floors to reach the {p:Home Point} on the twelfth floor. This will save you from having to ever do this climb again. Be advised that higher floors will contain enemies that are level 65+ and will aggro.
* Killing {m:Porphyrion} will also spawn a glowing ??? on the ground - interact with this to receive a key item version of the {@k} {k:Delkfutt key}. The glowing point will despawn when Porphyrion respawns.
** If you didn't collect the key item from the ???, you can trade your regular Delkfutt Key to the elevator on the floor at (H-8) inside {m:Porphyrion}'s room to receive the key item.
** If you didn't do that either, you can trade it to the Cermet Door on the first floor at (E-8).
** Once you have the key item version, you don't need the regular version of the key anymore. Technically it's used in a crafting quest later, but it's not hard to come back here for another one when you need it.
* Walk down the LONG staircase after using the elevator to get to the Basement.

=3 Finishing the Mission
* Once you reach the Basement head east into a large room and interact with the door at (L-7) with your newly obtained {@k} {k:Delkfutt key} for a cutscene.
** If you do not get the cutscene you are probably at the wrong door.
* Return to the **Windurstian Embassy** in {z:Ru'Lude Gardens}, let {n:Pakh Jatalfih} acknowledge your return then click the **Door: Windurstian Emb.** for a cutscene to complete the Mission.
** This is the 3rd door inside the embassy building. There are multiple doors with the same name.

=2 Notes
* You do not have to be on this Mission to receive a {@i:Delkfutt Key|549} {i:Delkfutt Key|Delkfutt Key|549} from {m:Porphyrion}.

